1
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:53,300
"Love is Better the Second Time Around season2"
(Episode 7)

2
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,359
Oh, by the way.

3
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,370
Miyata.

4
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,540
Have you decided on a
writer for next month's column?

5
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,740
I have someone in mind. I'm
setting up a meeting right now.

6
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,370
Good.

7
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:34,010
Director Tanabe wants someone
on Teacher Iwanaga's level,

8
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,920
but that's easier said than done.

9
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,590
Oh, right.

10
00:01:39,090 --> 00:01:42,180
Are Teacher Iwanaga's contract
cancellation forms ready?

11
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:44,770
We've been in touch via email.

12
00:01:45,060 --> 00:01:45,980
The terms have already been...

13
00:01:45,980 --> 00:01:46,640
I see.

14
00:01:46,890 --> 00:01:50,040
Could you go see Teacher Iwanaga in person
to get the final seal?

15
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:51,610
What?

16
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:55,380
After all, Teacher Iwanaga
has taken such good care of us.

17
00:01:55,690 --> 00:02:00,170
You'd like to see Teacher Iwanaga
one last time too, wouldn't you, Miyata?

18
00:02:57,170 --> 00:03:01,490
With this, the contract
termination is official.

19
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:26,170
Thank you so much

20
00:03:27,830 --> 00:03:29,680
for everything you've done for us.

21
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,260
Thank you as well.

22
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,010
I'll be on my way, then.

23
00:04:44,660 --> 00:04:46,660
Hey, you jerk.

24
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,040
A jerk...?

25
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,430
Can I help you?

26
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,480
How dare a guy like you

27
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:06,630
make Teacher Iwanaga cry!

28
00:05:09,300 --> 00:05:10,760
You complete jerk!

29
00:05:12,470 --> 00:05:15,220
Drowning in your own
pathetic inferiority complex,

30
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:19,290
blind to the immense
love right in front of you!

31
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:24,590
What kind of clueless
editor are you, anyway?!

32
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:30,010
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

33
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:45,380
Now that Teacher
Iwanaga's column has ended,

34
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:48,510
we'd like you to take
over, Professor Hibino.

35
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,140
That's why I came to see you.

36
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,660
All the way to Osaka?

37
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,100
Yes.

38
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:00,480
Did you think my guilt over
trying to come between you two

39
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:05,030
would make me take this job?

40
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:07,070
No, not at all.

41
00:06:07,490 --> 00:06:08,070
Well...

42
00:06:08,071 --> 00:06:09,551
You two already broke up, didn't you?

43
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:13,740
In that case,

44
00:06:14,350 --> 00:06:17,640
I have no reason to feel guilty anymore.

45
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,140
Please reconsider.

46
00:06:23,090 --> 00:06:26,520
Commercial writing doesn't suit me.

47
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:30,720
Please give it some thought.

48
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:35,160
Iwanaga is the right person for it.

49
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:39,750
Ending your relationship with him

50
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:41,540
was a mistake.

51
00:07:43,613 --> 00:07:46,350
[Iwanaga:] I noticed you
left something behind.

52
00:07:50,550 --> 00:07:51,940
I want to return it to you.

53
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:53,940
Can we meet up?

54
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:57,850
Tomorrow.

55
00:07:58,750 --> 00:08:00,180
I'll be waiting at Pier Park.

56
00:08:04,100 --> 00:08:06,870
I'm so sorry about what
happened the other day.

57
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:08,900
Please don't be.

58
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:11,490
I'm the one who should be
embarrassed for not noticing.

59
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:16,740
I had no idea you were Takashi's partner.

60
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:21,250
That's all in the past now.

61
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:26,590
Miyata.

62
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,920
Yes?

63
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:34,050
Actually, I saw you back in college.

64
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:36,760
What?

65
00:08:40,190 --> 00:08:41,770
During freshman year,

66
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:44,270
I met Takashi.

67
00:08:57,280 --> 00:08:59,700
Back then, he was always on his own.

68
00:08:59,990 --> 00:09:03,970
He had a look on his face like he'd
been abandoned by the entire world.

69
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:08,080
Hey.

70
00:09:08,410 --> 00:09:10,130
About the next statistics class...

71
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:13,020
I don't understand it at
all. Could you tutor me?

72
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:21,740
Thanks to you, I passed into the next year.

73
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:24,200
It's just a small token of appreciation,

74
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:27,390
but here's a thank-you gift.

75
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:28,650
Oh?

76
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:29,900
Can I open it?

77
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:30,900
Sure.

78
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,490
Thank you.

79
00:09:34,650 --> 00:09:35,820
Can I put it on?

80
00:09:37,450 --> 00:09:38,450
Thank you.

81
00:09:41,550 --> 00:09:42,909
Wait, don't tell me...

82
00:09:42,910 --> 00:09:43,620
Yeah.

83
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,700
It matches yours?

84
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,250
Yeah, it's a matching pair.

85
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:48,540
Thank you.

86
00:09:48,541 --> 00:09:49,750
I'll cherish it.

87
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:51,460
It looks great on you.

88
00:10:05,850 --> 00:10:06,850
Um...

89
00:10:11,610 --> 00:10:15,400
Takashi told me everything about his past.

90
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:17,910
About being adopted,

91
00:10:18,230 --> 00:10:19,660
changing his name,

92
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:21,850
and...

93
00:10:22,530 --> 00:10:23,890
about you.

94
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,350
You mean a trip?

95
00:10:47,350 --> 00:10:48,350
Yeah.

96
00:10:48,390 --> 00:10:49,940
To the beach,

97
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:52,230
or a hot spring.

98
00:10:52,310 --> 00:10:53,750
Since we finally have some time off.

99
00:10:54,730 --> 00:10:55,730
Sounds great.

100
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:59,910
If we do hot springs, I'd love
somewhere with a great night view.

101
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:03,370
Take a stroll at night,
then talk until dawn.

102
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:05,080
Until dawn?

103
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:28,980
I had never seen him look like that.

104
00:11:29,690 --> 00:11:33,480
That was when I first realized

105
00:11:33,950 --> 00:11:35,870
what Takashi looks like
when he's truly in love.

106
00:11:40,890 --> 00:11:41,890
Takashi...

107
00:11:43,700 --> 00:11:46,080
You're the only one he has ever loved.

108
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,640
I always thought...

109
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:14,310
I was the one always chasing,

110
00:12:15,730 --> 00:12:17,820
and always consumed by jealousy.

111
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,160
But...

112
00:12:24,570 --> 00:12:26,410
Senpai felt the exact same way,

113
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,560
and cared for me just as deeply.

114
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:42,020
Senpai! Wait!

115
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:46,320
Miyata...?

116
00:12:50,890 --> 00:12:52,090
I came to get...

117
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,690
what I left behind.

118
00:12:59,730 --> 00:13:01,170
What was it?

119
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:05,170
Me.

120
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,970
You left me behind.

121
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:13,870
The first time was at the station.

122
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:18,270
The second time was in that
apartment where we lived together.

123
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:27,680
I'm not strong enough
to go through this again and again.

124
00:13:30,510 --> 00:13:31,970
Neither am I.

125
00:13:32,900 --> 00:13:35,450
You told me before that
you couldn't trust me.

126
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,060
Why was that?

127
00:13:43,110 --> 00:13:45,840
Because I was terrified
of losing you again.

128
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:54,910
Arima-san told me everything.

129
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,420
Back in college,

130
00:13:58,710 --> 00:14:00,730
you saw me.

131
00:14:02,170 --> 00:14:04,300
If only you had told me back then,

132
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,720
maybe I could have been more honest,

133
00:14:10,890 --> 00:14:13,620
and trusted you completely.

134
00:14:15,270 --> 00:14:16,990
I was too young back then,

135
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,730
covered in scars.

136
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:22,870
If you had rejected me again,

137
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:26,880
I don't think I could have taken it.

138
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:33,970
Because you meant that much to me.

139
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:37,210
You do to me, too.

140
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:39,020
To me,

141
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,440
you are the only person in this world...

142
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:48,610
I have ever truly loved.

143
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,770
Miyata.

144
00:15:00,150 --> 00:15:01,830
I want to greet tomorrow morning,

145
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:04,420
and the morning after that,

146
00:15:06,530 --> 00:15:08,960
and thousands of mornings to come,

147
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,010
right by your side.

148
00:15:20,330 --> 00:15:22,640
Until the very end of our lives.

149
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,320
Will you stay with me forever?

150
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:39,600
I will.

151
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:43,040
Always.

152
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:45,570
Wherever we go,

153
00:15:48,110 --> 00:15:49,750
we'll always be together.

154
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:54,950
Takashi-san.

155
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:17,150
Well, look who it is.

156
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:18,900
Here comes the man of the hour!

157
00:19:19,350 --> 00:19:20,569
Thank you so much for everything.

158
00:19:20,570 --> 00:19:22,369
Not at all. Thank you.

159
00:19:22,370 --> 00:19:25,040
Look at this! Isn't it adorable?

160
00:19:25,050 --> 00:19:26,220
It really is.

161
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:31,390
Are you looking for someone?

162
00:19:31,710 --> 00:19:33,250
Oh, no, not really.

163
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,520
Here, please have a drink.

164
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,210
Thank you.

165
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:50,230
I heard they stuck to their guns
and convinced the company.

166
00:19:50,640 --> 00:19:53,900
Miyata has more backbone than I thought.

167
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:59,320
Though Tokyo Commerce probably didn't want
to burn bridges with Takashi either.

168
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:03,029
This Business Bear is Miyata-san, right?

169
00:20:03,030 --> 00:20:04,030
Yeah.

170
00:20:05,190 --> 00:20:09,370
I can't believe I lost to Miyata-san
in cuteness.

171
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:12,170
He brought your design to life beautifully.

172
00:20:12,420 --> 00:20:15,250
Give him a little credit, will you?

173
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:17,170
Fine.

174
00:20:17,171 --> 00:20:18,210
Good boy.

175
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,220
Congratulations.

176
00:20:21,300 --> 00:20:22,300
Thank you.

177
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:28,680
I'm sorry it ended up being
published by our company after all.

178
00:20:28,970 --> 00:20:30,180
Don't be ridiculous.

179
00:20:30,230 --> 00:20:31,640
After helping out this much,

180
00:20:31,890 --> 00:20:33,940
you'd better not leave me out now.

181
00:20:36,190 --> 00:20:37,190
Teacher Iwanaga.

182
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:39,290
It's about time for your speech.

183
00:20:39,570 --> 00:20:40,570
Right.

184
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:43,800
You too, Miyata.

185
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:45,030
Okay.

186
00:20:56,590 --> 00:20:59,460
Thank you all so much for coming today.

187
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:02,130
Though it was quite a bumpy road,

188
00:21:02,290 --> 00:21:08,410
we've finally published
'Finding Tomorrow's Value.'

189
00:21:11,290 --> 00:21:15,520
This book was created hand
in hand with my editor, Miyata.

190
00:21:15,810 --> 00:21:20,040
I hope it will be cherished
for a long time to come.

191
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,410
Also,

192
00:21:25,740 --> 00:21:27,720
there is one more thing
I'd like to announce.

193
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:33,540
This book isn't the only
thing that came to fruition.

194
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,720
Miyata and I...

195
00:21:49,300 --> 00:21:52,220
have officially become partners for life.

196
00:21:52,810 --> 00:21:53,350
What?

197
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:54,020
Huh?

198
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,690
Well, look at that.

199
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:04,320
For the rest of our lives,

200
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,820
we will support each
other every step of the way.

201
00:22:09,410 --> 00:22:12,080
Congratulations! Congratulations, you two!

202
00:22:13,990 --> 00:22:15,620
- Congratulations!
- Told you so.

203
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:22,500
Way to go, Miyata!

204
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:58,210
I'd really love to see
that apartment you bought.

205
00:22:58,370 --> 00:23:00,460
I haven't canceled the contract, you know.

206
00:23:01,130 --> 00:23:02,130
Really?

207
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:05,010
I figured you might change your mind.

208
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:06,880
I see.

209
00:23:07,930 --> 00:23:09,530
Want to stay there tonight?

210
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:11,800
Well...

211
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:16,280
Just you and me, the two of us who
pledged to spend our lives together.

212
00:23:17,770 --> 00:23:20,230
But I didn't bring any of my things.

213
00:23:20,350 --> 00:23:23,770
Besides, if we mess up the place,
won't that mean you can't cancel?

214
00:23:23,860 --> 00:23:25,490
Who knows?

215
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:27,860
Did you even read the contract?

216
00:23:27,950 --> 00:23:29,070
Skimmed it.

217
00:23:29,860 --> 00:23:32,200
This is why I call you
a spoiled rich kid...

218
00:23:32,890 --> 00:23:34,970
You really are so reliable.
